Z||000004||Monkeyman||08-14-2000||01:45 AM||||When I get ready to have my car painted, I plan on removing the lock cylinder and filling in the hole.  (I plan to move the battery to the front, first.)  I think it'll look trick (details count) and make it that much tougher to break into the trunk.  My wifes ex husband (she's still on good terms with him) is a whiz at painting and body work.  Only problem is that he lives 160 miles away.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaveL||08-14-2000||08:05 AM||||This is a problem that I've had once in a while. In my case I also noticed that every now and then I couldn't get the key to turn all the way to closed.(87 SE DIS 2.5 auto tranny) When this happens, I found that all I have to do is push up on my auto shifter knob, then I hear a click and all is well. I'm pretty sure the auto trunk lock is also hooked into the same relay. It won't allow the trunk to pop if the car is in gear, or the shifter isn't quite all the way up. Is yours an auto or a manual? I'm betting there is a similar arrangement for the manuals as well.||||reg||3
Z||000006||Xtreme Fiero's||08-14-2000||11:51 AM||||Monkeyman: I to have done that to my deck lid it does look prety cool. I used Moroso A/B puddy. But make sure you move the battery to the front, you are doomed if you don't and you leave your lights on or something.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
